   256	\paragraph{Availability.} The repository is public at \url{https://github.com/demirelo/touchstone-registered-tests} (release v2.1, archived at \url{https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24498973}), and its eight record files, with their SHA-\const{256} hashes, are archived at \url{https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24499068}. The release identifies the frozen evaluation code by the signed tag \texttt{protocol-v2} and preserves the original tagged-code report. It contains the code, the tuned files, all records of both tests (including incomplete, failed, and cut cells), the market generator, the block headers, the released H4 bundle, and the deviation evidence, and, separately dated, the decision-stability re-evaluation, the exploratory post hoc analyses with the per-seed evaluation and training inputs of the lottery analysis, the prediction-scoring correction with its regression test, the inference audit, the identity-replacement and churn follow-ups with their run records, the prospective-exploratory replication with its timestamped plan and manifest, block-hash draw, run records, analysis, and the record digest that its paper extract is checked against, and the paper sources. One command (\texttt{docs/revision/deviation/reproduce\_deviation.py}) checks the artifact against the tag and reproduces the second test's report under the disclosed configuration substitution; the paper's second-test tables and figures are regenerated from the tagged report, the disclosed stability output, and the exploratory post hoc and audit outputs by the scripts in \texttt{docs/revision/paper-v2}, \texttt{docs/revision/posthoc}, \texttt{docs/revision/audit}, \texttt{docs/revision/followup2}, and \texttt{docs/revision/followup3}, and the first test's records and verdict are in the release as recorded in October~\const{2026}.
