for C∗ minus R3 at p = 0.05 (“met”), for B3 minus R3 at 0.05 (“met”), for both at 0.03 (“met”),
and for the runner-up minus R3 at 0.05 (“met”), and R3’s audited share of the attacker’s jobs is
lower at 0.05 than without churn on at least five of six markets (“met”). The mean paired changes
are −0.146 (d), −0.142 (q), and −0.118 (u) at p = 0.05, and −0.063, −0.065, and −0.051 at 0.03.
