Lemma 2. R3’s priority list is ordered by age group, newest first. Within a group, the audit
keys are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables, so the group’s jobs
are exchangeable and the selected subset is uniform among them; delivery noise is independent of
selection.

Theorem 1. The spell length is geometric with mean 1/qE ; since survival to round t is determined
by earlier rounds, the expected spell profit is rE /qE . Adding the recovery’s rewards and entry charges
and dividing by the expected cycle length gives Π̄ by the renewal-reward theorem [33]. A cycle’s
surplus is at most (rE − h)/qE + ϵ ED; dividing by 1/qE + ED and using ED ≥ L gives the bound.

